{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098661-changeling-larger-than-life","id":1098661,"title":"Changeling, Larger Than Life","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-30T22:17:37-07:00","id":1098661,"title":"Changeling, Larger Than Life","content":"What if I would want to do something completely different? A game/setting with less changelings, but with each being a largely unique figure. Closer to Fables, Princes of Amber/Chaosites, somewhat (and maybe a bit of Exalted). Instead of being numerous species on a verge of extinction, Kithain being a bunch likeable Big Damn Heroes and Villains, capable of amassing giant armies, overthrowing kingdoms and delving deep into the Dreaming. Kicking some non-chimerical asses or producing epic magic, if needed. But on the flipside, having mortal lives to balance out all the magic and awesomeness, with powerful agents of Banality unwittingly trying to destroy everything of the Dreaming and Fae.<br /> <br /> How would you suggest to achieve that, setting and mechanics wise? Where to start?<br /> <br /> If you don't like this idea, there's no need to hammer it down. Just humour me, if you can. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-02-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T22:42:14-07:00","id":1098664,"title":"","content":"I'd use chuubos or Nobilis for the basis.. not many things work on two scales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T01:59:04-07:00","id":1098700,"title":"","content":"Gameplay-wise Nobilis is way more different than anything I would play so I won't even try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T06:22:43-07:00","id":1098742,"title":"","content":"In a mechanical sense just ramp up the amount of glamour available, multiplying the amount generated by freeholds so that it becomes plentiful, maybe lower the average banality of humanity. Metaphysically just set the dreaming back a few months seasonally. Tonally it's a big shift but you'd basically just need to figure out how to convert the setting to something more fables style. Maybe ditch the arcadian sidhe and make them all autumn just for solidarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T09:07:58-07:00","id":1098793,"title":"","content":"Allow Changelings and Kinain to recover one point of Glamour per hour of rest (similar to the Chi recovery of the Dhampyr of KotE).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T23:33:41-07:00","id":1099036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098661-changeling-larger-than-life?p=1098700#post1098700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gameplay-wise Nobilis is way more different than anything I would play so I won't even try.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the issue I've found generally with just powering things up is its VERY hard to make mortal lives not get overshadowed. Changeling gods of the Dreaming who can cast with relative impunity can change the world completely and not have to deal with crap. Its easy enough to power things up. Its hard to keep the mundane mattering though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:07:30-07:00","id":1099052,"title":"","content":"Obviously up the ante with Banal side of things, I'd say. If I'd make Freeholds shine brighter, as suggested, then I should make Autumn cut deeper.<br /> <br /> In Lost there was the matter of keeping up the Clarity as a requirement to not get bonkers, but I never played CtL. Actually, C20already does some of it with Nightmares, so it goes like that: You get metric ton of Nightmares, enough to need to retreat into your mundane life and to balance out the things you have to participate in some meaningful interactions with mortals and have your own life, because you are half-mortal, after all. But mundane life presents Banal pitfalls and dangers. Of course, you can overkill your problems away with faerie magic and martial prowess... but if your goal is to rest from the weirdness and magic it kinda defeats the purpose, so characters would have to approach things creatively.<br /> <br /> But easier said, than done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-01-2017, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:17:41-07:00","id":1099055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098661-changeling-larger-than-life?p=1099052#post1099052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously up the ante with Banal side of things, I'd say. If I'd make Freeholds shine brighter, as suggested, then I should make Autumn cut deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>At which point you've basically gone nowhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Lost there was the matter of keeping up the Clarity as a requirement to not get bonkers, but I never played CtL. Actually, C20already does some of it with Nightmares, so it goes like that: You get metric ton of Nightmares, enough to need to retreat into your mundane life and to balance out the things you have to participate in some meaningful interactions with mortals and have your own life, because you are half-mortal, after all. But mundane life presents Banal pitfalls and dangers. Of course, you can overkill your problems away with faerie magic and martial prowess... but if your goal is to rest from the weirdness and magic it kinda defeats the purpose, so characters would have to approach things creatively.<br /> <br /> But easier said, than done. </div> </div> </div>And you've basically circled back around to the game where it started no longer demigods of dream but once more having to hide from librarians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:21:54-07:00","id":1099058,"title":"","content":"Why not both? <br /> <br /> Like, if you can say, that 0+1-1 is the same thing, as 0+5-5, but for me it's not. Especially it is not. Especially if sometimes margin comes imbalanced. In eyes of Librarian-Who's-Dead-Inside character is another slacker, while in eyes of a Changeling, half of a district was trashed yesterday in a fight with a chimerical Kaiju and she knows it. At some point, she'll show them all, damnable Autumn People. But at the same time, they aren't worth it.<br /> <br /> Even Princes of Amber sometimes deal with mortals, and if pushed they can show off. But what they're actually terrifying at is their specialities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-01-2017, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:28:53-07:00","id":1099062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098661-changeling-larger-than-life?p=1099058#post1099058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you think C20 fails to give the option of being a pretty powerful creature especially if you gave them say an higher build? Rather than come up with a complicated setup of boosting changelings then boosting banality why not just give a bunch more points? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:55:00-07:00","id":1099075,"title":"","content":"Expanded my previous post.<br /> <br /> Firstly, they have to grow somewhere. Giving a bunch of points raises the advancement bar and a bunch of 10+ dice pools and character options isn't always a good thing. I'm a fan of &quot;Less is More&quot; design philosophy.<br /> <br /> Secondly, why do I always have a strong confrontational vibe from your posts? That's unwelcoming and not fun.<br /> As far as I'm aware, I never said, that I didn't consider giving more points. I even specifically said, that I'm not interested in devil advocates telling me, how this was a bad idea and here you are putting words into my mouth. Not cool, dude. Either chill it down a bit or reconsider answering to me.<br /> <br /> That's said, I'd love to talk about how it can be done. If you (any of you reading) have ideas, I'd love to hear/discuss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-01-2017, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:56:04-07:00","id":1099276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098661-changeling-larger-than-life?p=1099075#post1099075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanded my previous post.<br /> <br /> Firstly, they have to grow somewhere. Giving a bunch of points raises the advancement bar and a bunch of 10+ dice pools and character options isn't always a good thing. I'm a fan of &quot;Less is More&quot; design philosophy.<br /> <br /> Secondly, why do I always have a strong confrontational vibe from your posts? That's unwelcoming and not fun.<br /> As far as I'm aware, I never said, that I didn't consider giving more points. I even specifically said, that I'm not interested in devil advocates telling me, how this was a bad idea and here you are putting words into my mouth. Not cool, dude. Either chill it down a bit or reconsider answering to me.<br /> <br /> That's said, I'd love to talk about how it can be done. If you (any of you reading) have ideas, I'd love to hear/discuss them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am not tryign to be confrontational I am trying to understand what you want, i assumed you were disastified with &quot;Give them a bunch more xp&quot; since that's really the easiest solution. I'm also not sure how someone can kick nonchimerical ass without being able to kick Autumn folk ass. I mean for all the fluff of things being worse off than they have ever been for changelings they seem mechanically at their most powerful and have the easiest methods of obtaining glamour. So it might just be a matter of rephrasing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:44:32-07:00","id":1099295,"title":"","content":"Well, one option would be to give Changelings maximum Attributes and Abilities equal to their permanent Glamour (before modifications from their miens). You could then have Changelings with permanent Glamour 6+ (or the equivalent) with superhuman traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}